# One-shot `eval` works inside an evalLoop body, alongside `s.eval`.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val r = evalLoop[Int] { (ctx, s) => val a = eval[Int](\"3 + 4\"); s.complete(a) }"}
~ "ok":true.*val r: Int = 7

# A one-shot eval and a session line coexist in one body.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val r2 = evalLoop[Int] { (ctx, s) => s.eval(\"val x = 10\"); val a = eval[Int](\"100\"); val b = s.eval[Int](\"x\"); s.complete(a + b) }"}
~ "ok":true.*val r2: Int = 110
